ote\": \"Candidate A\"}", "thoughts": "We need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. As agent_1, we need to respond to the latest turn. The last turn was from Agent 3, providing observations on Candidate C and stating they continue to favor Candidate A. Now as Agent 1, we need to contribute next. We should consider the current state: All agents have shared observations. We have provisional votes all for Candidate A. Need to move discussion forward: maybe compare Candidate A vs Candidate C given new info, address unresolved issues like A's crew cooperation, D's hot temper effect, B's attention issues, etc. Perhaps ask for more info on D's hot temper effect on crew cooperation from Agent 2 (who has no info) or ask Agent 2 for any observations on D's crew cooperation. But we already asked Agent 2 earlier about D's hot temper effect and got \"No\". So that is resolved: no info. We might need to address A's crew cooperation: we have observations from Agent 3 that A is unfriendly, show-off, not open to ideas. That suggests poor crew cooperation. So we need to evaluate if A still best. Perhaps we should compare A vs C: C has strong crew cooperation but communication difficulty. A has strong technical but poor crew cooperation. Which is more critical? Likely crew cooperation is essential. So maybe we should reconsider recommendation. We could propose that Candidate C might be a stronger overall fit due to reliability, calmness, crew atmosphere, despite communication difficulty, which could be mitigated with training. So we could suggest shifting provisional vote to Candidate C, but need to discuss. However we must be evidence-based. We have evidence: C is 100% reliable, creates positive crew atmosphere, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention, calm, quick decisions. Weaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. A's weaknesses: unfriendly, show-off, not open to ideas, unorganized, resistant to criticism. Both have interpersonal issues. Which is more severe? A's show-off and unfriendly may directly affect crew cooperation; C's communication difficulty also affects. Might need to weigh. Perhaps we can propose a deeper comparison of A vs C on crew cooperation and communication, and ask if any panel member has observed A's ability to work with crew in simulations or real flights. Could ask Agent 2 (Markus) for any observations on A's crew cooperation beyond what we have. But we already have Agent 3's note that A is unfriendly. Maybe ask Agent 2 if they have any positive observations on A's crew cooperation. That could fill gap.\n\nThus as Agent 1, we can summarize current evidence, note that while A has strong technical, his interpersonal concerns are significant, and C shows strong crew cooperation but communication issues. Propose to discuss which set of concerns is more critical, and perhaps request any additional observations on A's crew cooperation from Agent 2.\n\nWe'll produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE summarizing and asking Agent 2 for any observations on Candidate A's crew cooperation/teamwork/professional communication (positive or negative). Then state provisional vote maybe still Candidate A but open to change.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: vote remains Candidate A.\n\nProceed."}
